Add an explicit Custom STT provider variant that talks to any OpenAI-compatible speech-to-text HTTP API.

## Goal
Operators can pin `stt.provider = \"custom\"` (never via auto) and point Hark at a base URL + API key + model. Product name is **Custom STT** — do not brand any specific gateway.

## API we adhere to (document in docs/PROVIDERS.md)
OpenAI-compatible batch STT surface only (no Realtime/WS):

- `POST {base_url}/audio/transcriptions`
- Auth: `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
- Content-Type: `multipart/form-data`
- Fields: `file` (wav bytes, filename `audio.wav`, type `audio/wav`), `model` (required), optional `language`
- Success response: JSON with `text` string (default OpenAI json shape)
- Errors: non-2xx → ProviderError with status + short body excerpt (no audio/token logging)

`base_url` is the OpenAI-style root including `/v1` (e.g. `https://gateway.example.com/v1`).

## Config / env
```toml
[stt]
provider = \"custom\"
custom_base_url = \"https://gateway.example.com/v1\"
# prefer env for secrets:
# custom_api_key = \"...\"   # optional; env wins
custom_model = \"gpt-4o-mini-transcribe\"  # or gateway-documented model id
```

| Env | Maps to |
|-----|---------|
| `HARK_STT_PROVIDER=custom` | pin |
| `HARK_STT_CUSTOM_BASE_URL` | base URL |
| `HARK_STT_CUSTOM_API_KEY` | bearer token |
| `HARK_STT_CUSTOM_MODEL` | model field |

## Acceptance
- [ ] `CustomStt` implements `SttProvider.transcribe`
- [ ] resolve_stt(\"custom\") requires base_url + key; clear errors if missing
- [ ] not selected by `auto`
- [ ] config load + config_to_dict round-trip
- [ ] unit tests with httpx mock (multipart shape, language, errors)
- [ ] docs/PROVIDERS.md documents Custom STT + API contract (no product-gateway branding)
- [ ] doctor / `hark providers` surface custom when configured (soft readiness: base_url+key present)
- [ ] CHANGELOG entry

## Out of scope (this ticket)
- Custom TTS
- Native dual-mount `/v1/stt` client path (OpenAI `/audio/transcriptions` only)
- Streaming STT